. also matches a newline (PCRE2’s DOTALL), and $ matches only at the very end rather than before a final newline (DOLLAR_ENDONLY);
a backslash inside a bracket expression is a literal, so [\d] is a backslash or a d, not a digit;

\&lt; and \&gt; are word boundaries (\b(?=\w) and \b(?&lt;=\w));
in UTF-8 text, \w, \b and POSIX classes such as [[:alpha:]] follow Unicode (PCRE2’s UCP), as TRE’s wide-character classes do.
